Resource policies
A few resources in AWS, such as Amazon S3 buckets and IAM roles, also have a resource policy.
These constructs have an addToResourcePolicy method (Python: add_to_resource_policy),
which takes a PolicyStatement as its argument. Every policy statement added to a resource
policy must specify at least one principal.
In the following example, the Amazon S3 bucket bucket grants a role with the s3:SomeAction
permission to itself.
