Running your app
The CDK CLI needs to know how to run your CDK app. If you created the project from a
template using the cdk init command, your app’s cdk.json file includes an app key.
This key specifies the necessary command for the language that the app is written in. If your
language requires compilation, the command line performs this step before running the app
automatically.
Example
TypeScript
{
"app": "npx ts-node --prefer-ts-exts bin/my-app.ts"
}
JavaScript
{
"app": "node bin/my-app.js"
}
Python
{
"app": "python app.py"
}
Java
{
"app": "mvn -e -q compile exec:java"
}
